{
  "version": "workflow-synthetic-200-v1",
  "method": "current-assessment-led-position-specific-v1",
  "description": "200 fictional student scenarios across four isolated program frameworks. Each program has ten fixed evidence patterns, repeated over five location variants. Results test software behavior and reference-label agreement, not population accuracy or placement success.",
  "sources": {
    "DNSC": {
      "title": "DNSC program offerings",
      "url": "https://dnsc.edu.ph/program-offerings/",
      "use": "Program/institute names and general program context; not numeric thresholds."
    },
    "WEB": {
      "title": "O*NET Web Developers 15-1254.00",
      "url": "https://www.onetonline.org/link/summary/15-1254.00",
      "use": "Web development, code review, browser compatibility and interface duties."
    },
    "NETWORK": {
      "title": "O*NET Network and Computer Systems Administrators 15-1244.00",
      "url": "https://www.onetonline.org/link/summary/15-1244.00",
      "use": "Networks, troubleshooting, records, backups and access/security duties."
    },
    "SOCIAL": {
      "title": "O*NET Social and Human Service Assistants 21-1093.00",
      "url": "https://www.onetonline.org/link/summary/21-1093.00",
      "use": "Supervised intake, service referral, group support, documentation and monitoring examples."
    },
    "FRONT": {
      "title": "TESDA Front Office Services NC II",
      "url": "https://www.tesda.gov.ph/Downloadables/TR%20Front%20Office%20Services%20NC%20II.pdf",
      "use": "Reservations, reception, customer service and workplace communication examples; 2013 amended document."
    },
    "TRAVEL": {
      "title": "TESDA Travel Services NC II Revision 01",
      "url": "https://tesda.gov.ph/Downloadables/Travel%20Services%20NC%20II.pdf",
      "use": "Travel requests, reservations/transactions, documentation and related records; promulgated 2019."
    }
  },
  "notes": [
    "All students, answers, partners and internship openings are fictional.",
    "Skills and duties are adapted from referenced occupational/training material; question wording is newly authored for software testing.",
    "Numeric minima, scores and expected-role labels are developer-authored test assumptions, not official DNSC, TESDA or O*NET thresholds.",
    "No real student records, questions, answers or placements are read or changed.",
    "Each observed category combines two synthetic assessment point totals (maximum 30 and 70), not an average of percentages. Missing categories remain absent.",
    "Five location variants repeat each evidence pattern; these are 200 student scenarios, not 200 independent proficiency samples.",
    "Expected roles were authored before model inference. The equal-score reference case uses role 0 as a reviewable label; NLP/location may legitimately prefer another role.",
    "All-zero evidence expects no recommendation. Gate agreement is included in overall agreement and disclosed separately.",
    "Synthetic categories and minima are examples for testing; they do not prescribe live program curricula."
  ],
